# Configuration reference: Nginx reverse proxy

```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name app.example.com;

    ssl_certificate     /etc/ssl/app.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/ssl/app.key;

    client_max_body_size 25m;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://app_upstream;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_read_timeout 60s;
    }
}

upstream app_upstream {
    server 10.0.0.10:8000;
    server 10.0.0.11:8000;
    keepalive 32;
}
```

## Directives
| Directive | Context | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `listen` | server | Address, port, and TLS/http2 flags |
| `server_name` | server | Hostnames this block answers |
| `proxy_pass` | location | Upstream target |
| `proxy_read_timeout` | location | Wait for the upstream body |
| `client_max_body_size` | server | Reject larger uploads with 413 |
| `keepalive` | upstream | Pooled connections to backends |

## Notes
Always set `X-Forwarded-Proto` so the app builds correct redirect URLs. `keepalive` requires HTTP/1.1 to the upstream.

# Configuration reference: backend and provider

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.6"
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = "acme-tfstate"
    key            = "prod/network.tfstate"
    region         = "us-east-1"
    dynamodb_table = "acme-tf-lock"
    encrypt        = true
  }
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 5.40"
    }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
  default_tags {
    tags = { ManagedBy = "terraform" }
  }
}
```

## Arguments
| Argument | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `required_version` | Terraform CLI constraint |
| `backend.s3.bucket` / `key` | State location |
| `dynamodb_table` | State locking table |
| `encrypt` | Encrypt state at rest |
| `required_providers.*.version` | `~> 5.40` allows 5.x but not 6.0 |
| `default_tags` | Applied to every resource unless overridden |

## Notes
Never use a local backend for shared infrastructure. `terraform init -migrate-state` moves state when the backend changes.
